WEBVTT

00:06.631 --> 00:08.341
[sweet airy music]

00:43.376 --> 00:45.045
[sucks in breath]

00:45.128 --> 00:46.296
Oh, things I hate?

00:47.756 --> 00:49.174
It's still Kook Yeon-su.

00:50.425 --> 00:52.886
And I can give you over ten reasons
why I hate her.

00:53.470 --> 00:57.182
[Ung] First off, as I'm sure you know,
she can be so selfish.

00:57.265 --> 01:01.019
Yeon-su, you think we can see your notes
from our last class?

01:01.102 --> 01:03.021
[girl 1] I hear that
it's gonna be on the test.

01:03.855 --> 01:05.023
[sighs]

01:05.106 --> 01:06.941
And you're the only one who took notes.

01:08.568 --> 01:10.612
Our test's tomorrow.
Can't you help us out?

01:10.695 --> 01:12.655
[girl 2] Besides,
we'll give it back right away.

01:12.739 --> 01:14.032
[sighs]

01:17.869 --> 01:20.080
[cheeky music]

01:20.163 --> 01:21.790
[paper rustling]

01:23.958 --> 01:26.044
There, I don't have my notes anymore.

01:26.127 --> 01:27.629
Can you two go now?

01:27.712 --> 01:30.381
- I knew she was really stuck-up.
- Gosh.

01:31.007 --> 01:32.675
[girl 1] Man, she's so unbelievable.

01:32.759 --> 01:33.843
[groans]

01:37.138 --> 01:40.016
Hello, I'm Kook Yeon-su,
and I'm the team leader of Group 2.

01:40.099 --> 01:42.185
- 674 DAYS OF DATING
- And my team is…

01:43.436 --> 01:44.270
THE BROTHERS KARAMAZOV

01:44.354 --> 01:45.271
GROUP 2 KOOK YEON-SU

01:45.355 --> 01:47.273
- …it's just me.
- [shocked mumbling]

01:47.357 --> 01:49.025
Let me start the presentation.

01:49.108 --> 01:52.862
[Yeon-su] I will be making a presentation
on Book 12, or "A Judicial Error."

01:52.946 --> 01:54.614
[Ung] And she doesn't have that much…

01:54.697 --> 01:57.408
I mean, she has no social skills at all.

01:57.492 --> 02:00.870
FEBRUARY 20, 2012
215 DAYS OF DATING

02:02.539 --> 02:03.373
[groans]

02:03.957 --> 02:05.416
Come on, let's drink more today.

02:05.500 --> 02:07.377
Don't worry, I'll take you home.
It'll be okay.

02:07.961 --> 02:10.130
And what made you think
you'll take me home?

02:10.213 --> 02:11.589
Well, I can drink better than you.

02:11.673 --> 02:14.384
- You can't be sure of that.
- Hey, come on, I'm a guy after all.

02:15.009 --> 02:15.885
Let's see, then.

02:17.095 --> 02:19.055
- What?
- Let's see who can drink more.

02:19.639 --> 02:21.224
[Ung] She tries to win at everything.

02:21.307 --> 02:22.267
You really mean it?

02:23.351 --> 02:25.270
[customer] More drinks, please. Two beers.

02:28.606 --> 02:31.192
Hey, wait, look, we only came here
to have some fun, didn't we?

02:31.276 --> 02:32.110
Drink up.

02:32.694 --> 02:35.280
[cheery music]

02:37.448 --> 02:38.867
All right. You win, that's far enough.

02:41.744 --> 02:44.080
[Ung] This competitive spirit of hers
is so useless.…

02:44.164 --> 02:46.624
You know, sometimes
you don't act like a senior.

02:46.708 --> 02:48.001
It's so ridiculous.

02:48.084 --> 02:51.045
Is that all you have to show off?
Being my senior? Is that all, huh?

02:51.129 --> 02:54.799
- [guy] Looks like we coddled you.
- "Coddled me"? When did you ever do that?

02:54.883 --> 02:57.552
What do you think I am? Your dog, huh?
What am I, your granddaughter?

02:57.635 --> 02:58.553
What the hell did you say?

02:58.636 --> 03:01.347
- I'm sorry. She's just a bit worked up.
- Why would you apologize? Move.

03:01.431 --> 03:03.141
- Why don't you say that again?
- [Ung] She picks fights

03:03.224 --> 03:04.475
with nearly everyone.

03:04.559 --> 03:05.393
Move it.

03:06.603 --> 03:09.314
[Ung] And don't get me started
on how stubborn she is.

03:10.440 --> 03:13.401
Have you lost your mind?
Why would I get a haircut like that?

03:13.484 --> 03:14.652
Why not? It looks all right.

03:14.736 --> 03:16.654
Do you really think
curly hair would suit me?

03:17.447 --> 03:20.033
- Why don't you look like this then?
- I'm sorry?

03:20.116 --> 03:21.159
Do his hair like this.

03:23.244 --> 03:26.289
His hair is too short.
I won't be able to do this hairstyle.

03:26.372 --> 03:28.041
No, it's all right.
Just make sure you do it.

03:28.124 --> 03:29.918
Hey, wait a second,
it's my hair, you know.

03:30.001 --> 03:32.337
Since yesterday, my ideal type
has been someone who can pull this off.

03:32.921 --> 03:33.755
I'm not doing this.

03:33.838 --> 03:34.923
Please, do what you can.

03:35.006 --> 03:36.007
FAITH HAIR SALON

03:36.841 --> 03:37.675
[sighs]

03:39.928 --> 03:41.137
[Ung] She's a psychopath

03:41.221 --> 03:44.557
who has to do whatever she wants,
no matter what I said.

03:45.475 --> 03:46.935
Can't you take the day off?

03:47.477 --> 03:50.730
[Yeon-su] I can't. It's not even
something that important anyway.

03:50.813 --> 03:53.107
Today's the last day
to see the cherry blossoms.

03:54.442 --> 03:56.236
This is our last chance.
It'll rain tomorrow.

03:56.319 --> 03:59.781
Why would we go all that way
just to see cherry blossoms?

04:00.406 --> 04:02.283
- And besides, there's next year.
- What?

04:02.367 --> 04:04.661
But that's what you said last year.
So why not go this year?

04:04.744 --> 04:07.789
And they're the prettiest
right before they start falling too.

04:07.872 --> 04:10.208
[Yeon-su] Why would you see flowers
that are about to fall?

04:10.291 --> 04:11.376
They don't even have a scent

04:11.459 --> 04:14.629
so they're just useless flowers
with bunched-up petals.

04:14.712 --> 04:15.797
[sighs deeply]

04:16.673 --> 04:20.635
[Ung] And more than that,
she has no sense of romance at all.

04:21.678 --> 04:24.055
Hmm… So how many are left?

04:24.138 --> 04:25.807
- Hey, Yeon-su!
- Yes?

04:26.391 --> 04:29.185
- Hey, you said you'd eat lunch with me.
- Oh, right.

04:29.269 --> 04:32.146
Go eat with your friend. I have to go
to the library to fix my assignment.

04:32.230 --> 04:33.356
What?

04:33.439 --> 04:37.277
I came to school to have lunch with you
when I didn't even have class.

04:37.360 --> 04:39.028
Just eat with him.
This assignment's important.

04:39.612 --> 04:41.197
- Bye. I'll text you later.
- Hey.

04:41.281 --> 04:42.991
[Ung] She always
has important stuff to do.

04:44.367 --> 04:46.452
I hate that she only thinks about herself.

04:46.536 --> 04:49.163
Is she your girlfriend? Oh, so that's her.

04:49.247 --> 04:50.999
She's famous in our school.

04:51.082 --> 04:53.876
She's pretty and all,
but her personality is…

04:53.960 --> 04:56.212
[sighs]
How can you date someone like her?

04:56.296 --> 04:59.382
Hey, do you even know
anything about Yeon-su?

04:59.465 --> 05:01.759
- What?
- Don't talk about her like that.

05:02.844 --> 05:04.053
You don't know anything.

05:06.014 --> 05:07.932
[Ung] And here's another thing I hate…

05:08.558 --> 05:13.104
AUGUST 31, 2011
42 DAYS OF DATING

05:13.187 --> 05:15.189
[light music]

05:16.149 --> 05:17.608
- This…
- Mm-hmm.

05:17.692 --> 05:20.486
And this. They'll be on the test,
so go over them.

05:20.570 --> 05:22.822
And read through this
at least three times, okay?

05:22.905 --> 05:24.741
- Okay.
- I'm going to check.

05:27.660 --> 05:30.163
[Ung] …that is
only I know one side of Yeon-su

05:31.789 --> 05:33.082
that nobody else knows.

05:33.583 --> 05:35.335
[Yeon-su] This is way more fun
than hanging out with Ung,

05:35.418 --> 05:37.253
- I'll tell you that much.
- [both chuckle]

05:38.671 --> 05:40.840
[Yeon-ok] Ung isn't really
a fun guy to hang out with, right?

05:40.923 --> 05:42.550
[Yeon-su] He can be
a real snore sometimes.

05:42.633 --> 05:44.343
- "A snore"?
- Oh, we call boring people "snores."

05:44.844 --> 05:47.346
- [Yeon-ok] Oh.
- Mom. I can hear everything.

05:48.056 --> 05:49.807
[Yeon-ok] Mr. Snore has good ears, though.

05:49.891 --> 05:52.060
- [Yeon-ok] Thank you so much, Mr. Snore.
- Of course.

05:52.894 --> 05:55.063
- [Yeon-ok] Let's eat before we continue.
- [both chuckle]

05:55.146 --> 05:58.608
FEBRUARY 20, 2012
215 DAYS OF DATING

05:58.691 --> 06:00.068
- Hop on.
- [grunts]

06:01.652 --> 06:02.820
[groaning]

06:02.904 --> 06:04.989
[light sweet music]

06:09.202 --> 06:11.913
JUNE 4, 2012
320 DAYS OF DATING

06:15.291 --> 06:18.544
If you guys ever do that to Ung again,
I won't let it slide.

06:18.628 --> 06:21.714
Did you think I wouldn't notice you
ordering him around like an errand boy

06:21.798 --> 06:22.965
just because he's too nice?

06:23.549 --> 06:25.343
If you ever do that to him again,

06:25.426 --> 06:27.428
I'll show you how crazy I can really be.

06:29.263 --> 06:31.224
APRIL 1, 2013
621 DAYS OF DATING

06:32.391 --> 06:33.476
[sighs]

06:37.146 --> 06:38.564
So why did you wanna see me?

06:39.482 --> 06:41.067
- [Yeon-su] Are you upset?
- Who? Me?

06:41.150 --> 06:44.821
- No way. Why? Should I be, huh?
- [scoffs]

06:44.904 --> 06:46.572
[Yeon-su] We eat lunch
together all the time,

06:46.656 --> 06:48.616
- so why get upset over one meal?
- Well…

06:49.408 --> 06:52.912
- It's not exactly just one meal.
- Were you counting? That's so petty.

06:52.995 --> 06:55.873
Petty? Did you just call me petty?
[groans]

06:57.333 --> 06:58.960
Hey. What's up?

07:01.045 --> 07:04.423
[gentle sweet music]

07:12.723 --> 07:15.184
[Yeon-su] Here are the cherry blossoms.
We saw them.

07:17.145 --> 07:19.230
[Ung] She showed
this side of her only to me.

07:20.565 --> 07:22.316
So I can't help but love her.

07:26.612 --> 07:27.905
And the ninth reason…

07:27.989 --> 07:29.532
She makes me love her… 

07:30.992 --> 07:34.036
but then just when I'm about
to love her even more…

07:35.913 --> 07:38.166
Why do we have to break up?

07:40.001 --> 07:42.712
[Ung] When I think
I couldn't be any happier…

07:42.795 --> 07:44.797
You always break up with me first.

07:47.800 --> 07:51.220
[Ung] …she would take me
to the highest of places first…

07:51.304 --> 07:54.849
Am I the easiest thing
to throw away of all the things you have?

07:58.519 --> 07:59.604
No.

08:01.439 --> 08:03.608
[Ung] …and then she pushes me off.

08:04.442 --> 08:05.818
But you're the only one…

08:08.571 --> 08:10.156
that I can get rid of.

08:11.616 --> 08:13.659
[soft somber music]

08:13.743 --> 08:15.786
[Ung] She is so cruel.

08:17.205 --> 08:19.248
["There For You" by Kim Na Young playing]

08:45.525 --> 08:47.902
["There For You"
by Kim Na Young continues]

09:07.672 --> 09:09.757
What if I had stopped behaving childishly?

09:12.552 --> 09:14.136
Would you have stayed with me?

09:20.893 --> 09:24.564
If you were being sincere back then,
tell me, what would you have done?

09:26.023 --> 09:28.109
[melancholic music]

09:28.985 --> 09:30.903
[deep sigh]

09:42.498 --> 09:46.377
10 THINGS I HATE ABOUT YOU

09:46.460 --> 09:51.757
EPISODE 3

09:56.012 --> 09:57.221
IT'S BEEN 10 YEARS
IT'S BLOWING UP AGAIN

09:57.305 --> 09:58.472
[Sol-i] I'm a friend of Yeon-su.

09:58.556 --> 10:00.808
She does have a bad temper,
but she's kind.

10:00.891 --> 10:01.976
And to be honest,

10:02.059 --> 10:05.229
Choi Ung's the one who usually gets
a rise out of people and picks fights.

10:05.313 --> 10:06.480
[scoffs]

10:08.608 --> 10:10.943
[Eun-ho] What?
Choi Ung's just a bit weird.

10:11.027 --> 10:13.779
But he isn't the type to pick fights.
You're making it up.

10:13.863 --> 10:16.240
[quirky music]

10:16.324 --> 10:17.867
[Sol-i] Do you even know the guy?

10:17.950 --> 10:20.578
"Just a bit weird"?
I think he's very weird.

10:20.661 --> 10:22.288
You're the one who's making things up.

10:23.539 --> 10:24.915
[Eun-ho] You're ridiculous.

10:24.999 --> 10:27.585
You'd be shocked
if you knew how he's doing lately.

10:27.668 --> 10:29.128
He's really successful, you know.

10:29.211 --> 10:31.422
He's a famous artist. Jeez.

10:32.048 --> 10:33.883
- [groaning]
- Hey, Ung, did you get some sleep?

10:33.966 --> 10:35.760
[Eun-ho] Is there a mosquito here?

10:37.178 --> 10:38.012
[Sol-i] What's he doing, then?

10:38.095 --> 10:41.349
I'm sure he won't be as successful
as our smart Yeon-su.

10:41.849 --> 10:42.975
[scoffs]

10:44.560 --> 10:46.937
[Eun-ho] He was only
pretending to be dull.

10:47.021 --> 10:49.482
He's earning loads of money,
and he's a successful…

10:50.608 --> 10:52.234
- Hey. What are you doing?
- [crackles]

10:52.318 --> 10:53.402
[groans]

10:54.320 --> 10:55.529
[sighs]

10:55.613 --> 10:58.449
[Eun-ho] But he might have
the brains of a mosquito.

10:58.532 --> 11:00.326
[clears throat]
Hey…

11:01.285 --> 11:03.329
Eun-ho, how's my schedule looking?

11:04.789 --> 11:07.291
Nothing much except your exhibit. Why?

11:07.375 --> 11:08.459
- Really?
- Wait.

11:08.542 --> 11:10.252
Are you going to do the drawing show?

11:11.629 --> 11:14.840
Hey, why don't you get me some more work
to do? I've rested for too long.

11:14.924 --> 11:17.927
All of a sudden? You said
you wanted to take things slow.

11:18.010 --> 11:19.428
I need a distraction.

11:20.471 --> 11:21.972
- What?
- You're not

11:22.056 --> 11:24.683
going to stay cooped up in your room
working like before, are you?

11:24.767 --> 11:26.685
No, I won't. I won't do that again.

11:26.769 --> 11:28.229
But get me a lot of work.

11:28.312 --> 11:30.940
And I'll think about the drawing show.
It's still a maybe.

11:31.732 --> 11:32.650
All right then.

11:33.401 --> 11:35.528
But Ung, you have to get
plenty of sleep too.

11:36.153 --> 11:38.155
Your insomnia seems to have gotten worse.

11:39.824 --> 11:41.367
[sighs deeply]

11:42.493 --> 11:44.370
I guess it's still summer after all.

11:47.081 --> 11:49.166
YOU'D BE SHOCKED IF YOU KNEW
HOW HE'S DOING LATELY

11:50.835 --> 11:53.671
COMMENTS

11:56.048 --> 11:57.425
- [Yeon-su] What's up?
- Hmm?

11:58.467 --> 11:59.468
It's nothing.

12:03.264 --> 12:05.724
- Hey, Sol-i, I…
- Hmm?

12:07.560 --> 12:09.311
Never mind. Forget about it.

12:10.229 --> 12:12.064
[chuckles]

12:12.565 --> 12:15.860
You know, they say there are two ways
to make people go crazy.

12:15.943 --> 12:18.696
The first is to stop
in the middle of a sentence, and--

12:18.779 --> 12:20.114
I met Ung a while ago.

12:22.241 --> 12:24.910
Well, what I meant to say was,
I went to see him.

12:26.954 --> 12:29.457
You? Why? What for?

12:30.916 --> 12:32.668
- Wait, do you still--
- No way!

12:33.252 --> 12:35.171
There was someone I had to meet.

12:35.254 --> 12:37.423
It was supposed to be
for a project at work,

12:37.506 --> 12:38.883
and it turned out to be him.

12:38.966 --> 12:40.301
- [gasps]
- [Yeon-su] Funny, huh?

12:41.969 --> 12:43.429
Is this real?

12:43.512 --> 12:46.140
Why him, though? What's he doing now?

12:46.223 --> 12:48.309
Is he really successful, as people say?

12:48.392 --> 12:52.062
Well, I don't know how he lives,
but it looks like he did succeed.

12:52.897 --> 12:56.734
Wow. The guy who was
always lying down in the shade?

12:58.027 --> 13:00.529
Wow, life is full of surprises, isn't it?

13:03.532 --> 13:05.826
And so? How did it go?

13:06.827 --> 13:08.370
- What did?
- [Sol-i] You know.

13:08.871 --> 13:10.789
How was it seeing him again?

13:11.540 --> 13:13.542
- I really didn't feel anything.
- [scoffs]

13:13.626 --> 13:14.960
Hey.

13:15.044 --> 13:17.671
You're obviously lying.
I can tell, you know.

13:17.755 --> 13:19.965
I mean, when someone
so much as says the name of my ex,

13:20.049 --> 13:21.550
I can feel my heart drop to my feet.

13:21.634 --> 13:23.135
There's no way you felt nothing then.

13:23.219 --> 13:25.679
Don't you have way too many exes
to feel that, though?

13:25.763 --> 13:27.181
Oh, shut up. Anyway,

13:27.264 --> 13:29.350
being way too cool
about that isn't normal.

13:29.433 --> 13:31.352
Well, I really am cool about it.

13:31.435 --> 13:33.562
You know I don't hold grudges or anything.

13:33.646 --> 13:36.273
[phone buzzing]

13:41.779 --> 13:42.780
Yes, hello?

13:45.074 --> 13:46.158
Kim Ji-ung?

13:48.369 --> 13:50.162
What? What do you want me to do?

13:50.788 --> 13:51.705
[set chatter]

13:51.789 --> 13:54.166
[Ung] Kook Yeon-su! You psycho!

13:54.750 --> 13:55.668
[chuckles softly]

13:57.586 --> 13:58.796
- [NJ] I mean, look.
- [Mi-yeon] Looking at that again?

13:58.879 --> 14:01.465
Go-oh was acting all quiet and nice.

14:01.549 --> 14:04.343
Kook Yeon-su! You psycho!

14:04.426 --> 14:06.512
He's cute I guess,
but he looks a bit dumb, huh?

14:06.595 --> 14:10.182
I know, right? So how can I resist
a cute, simple guy like him?

14:10.266 --> 14:11.475
COMMENTS
NJGODDESS

14:11.559 --> 14:13.852
That's a nice username you've got there.

14:13.936 --> 14:16.146
But why did he film something like that?

14:16.230 --> 14:18.607
I don't know.
But the guy sure is full of surprises.

14:19.191 --> 14:21.026
[NJ] There's no way he can bore me.

14:21.110 --> 14:23.028
[chuckles softly]
Where's Chi-seong?

14:23.112 --> 14:24.822
Oh, the CEO called him.

14:24.905 --> 14:27.449
Why? What's going on?

14:29.577 --> 14:31.203
What is it? Just tell me.

14:32.162 --> 14:34.748
I think it's because of your live video.
The one from yesterday.

14:35.833 --> 14:36.876
What about it?

14:36.959 --> 14:38.627
[Mi-yeon] People who
don't even know you at all

14:39.211 --> 14:43.340
must've spread rumors about you
being depressed or on some hard drugs.

14:43.924 --> 14:45.301
There were some articles about it.

14:45.384 --> 14:48.596
If our CEO calls, you or Chi-seong
can just tell me right away.

14:48.679 --> 14:49.638
I'm gonna go now.
[sighs]

14:50.848 --> 14:51.765
Okay.

14:52.474 --> 14:54.059
[phone buzzing]

14:54.143 --> 14:55.561
Just turn it off.

14:55.644 --> 14:56.604
[Mi-yeon] All right.

14:58.689 --> 14:59.815
[gasps]

14:59.899 --> 15:01.692
- Wait, who is it?
- "Choi Un--"

15:03.736 --> 15:05.863
[gasps]
He called me.

15:05.946 --> 15:07.656
[crew] All right.
Let's get back to filming!

15:07.740 --> 15:09.742
Could I just have five min…
I mean, ten minutes?

15:09.825 --> 15:11.452
[phone continues buzzing]

15:12.077 --> 15:13.078
MR. CHOI UNG

15:13.704 --> 15:15.039
[clears throat]

15:15.122 --> 15:16.498
[steadying breath]

15:17.082 --> 15:18.125
MR. CHOI UNG

15:19.335 --> 15:23.172
Hi, I'm sorry I answered a bit late,
but I was busy with my shoot.

15:23.255 --> 15:24.757
What did you wanna talk to me about?

15:25.758 --> 15:26.759
Hello, you there?

15:28.594 --> 15:29.720
Mr. Choi?

15:31.180 --> 15:33.474
[quirky music]

15:34.725 --> 15:36.518
MR. CHOI UNG

15:38.395 --> 15:40.564
- [spraying]
- [phone buzzing]

15:42.358 --> 15:43.192
[Ung] Yes, hello?

15:43.275 --> 15:45.569
[NJ] Why did you hang up so quickly?
That was so rude of you.

15:45.653 --> 15:48.906
- It was the first time you called me.
- Oh, did I? Sorry.

15:48.989 --> 15:51.533
Yes, and I can't believe
you hung up on me.

15:51.617 --> 15:53.577
- [chuckles awkwardly]
- So why did you call me?

15:53.661 --> 15:57.373
Well, that thing you asked for last time.
Drawing your buildings and…

15:57.456 --> 15:58.332
Oh, so you'll do it?

15:58.415 --> 16:00.417
Yes, but then…

16:01.001 --> 16:02.920
I've always drawn whatever I wanted to,

16:03.003 --> 16:05.214
I've never gotten
a request from anyone before.

16:05.297 --> 16:07.633
I think I'll be able to decide
after seeing your buildings.

16:07.716 --> 16:08.676
Sure, that's all right.

16:08.759 --> 16:11.220
Well then, why don't we go see them now?

16:11.804 --> 16:13.639
Well, I think I'll be busy today.

16:14.640 --> 16:16.266
And aren't you busy on your shoot too?

16:16.350 --> 16:18.143
- I am, but I'm not.
- What?

16:18.227 --> 16:20.896
Anyway, I'm busy, but I'm not too.
So tell me, when are you free?

16:21.939 --> 16:25.401
Oh, then I'll get back to you
after checking my sched.

16:25.484 --> 16:28.112
Shouldn't I be the one
telling you I'll check my schedule?

16:28.195 --> 16:30.406
[NJ] I'm the celebrity here.
This kinda feels wrong.

16:30.489 --> 16:32.616
NJ! The director says
we have to start filming.

16:34.118 --> 16:36.996
Anyway, get back to me later.
And it'd better be real soon, got it?

16:37.079 --> 16:40.457
I hate it when people say
they'll contact me and take a long time.

16:41.041 --> 16:42.084
Bye, then.

16:42.167 --> 16:43.210
- Alright.
- [phone chimes]

16:44.044 --> 16:45.504
Holy mother of…
[groans]

16:45.587 --> 16:47.673
[Eun-ho] You told me to get you more work.

16:47.756 --> 16:50.467
But then I catch you calling NJ yourself
when I'm your manager!

16:50.551 --> 16:51.593
Oh, jeez.

16:52.219 --> 16:54.388
Are you really pissed off about that?

16:54.471 --> 16:56.807
What? Seriously?

16:56.890 --> 16:58.767
Wow! You're unbelievable, man!

16:58.851 --> 17:00.936
I can't believe
you've really changed, Ung.

17:01.020 --> 17:02.688
Now that you're contacting NJ in person,

17:02.771 --> 17:04.606
you think you're
a hot shot artist or something?

17:04.690 --> 17:06.275
Is that how you see yourself now?

17:07.067 --> 17:09.445
Well, a word of advice,
you're gonna get a lot of hate.

17:09.528 --> 17:11.280
Both from me, and NJ's fans.

17:11.363 --> 17:14.324
Trust me when I say that
everyone's going to hate you now.

17:14.408 --> 17:15.868
- [spraying]
- Shut up, man.

17:16.827 --> 17:18.162
I've got a job for you to do.

17:19.371 --> 17:21.457
What is it? Are you going to meet NJ now?

17:21.540 --> 17:22.624
Should I get the car?

17:25.419 --> 17:27.212
[Eun-ho] I'm your manager,

17:27.838 --> 17:29.965
not your slave. You understand?

17:30.049 --> 17:32.134
Did you hear me?
Gosh, do I really have to do this?

17:32.217 --> 17:34.720
[Ung] If you have a conscience,
you'd do what I tell you.

17:35.304 --> 17:38.057
Do I have to remind you
how many days you've stayed in my house?

17:38.140 --> 17:40.100
Seriously? Come on,
I can't believe you kept count.

17:40.184 --> 17:41.268
It was only a few days and--

17:41.351 --> 17:45.105
[Ung] Hey, hey. You completely
emptied my fridge, remember?

17:45.189 --> 17:46.607
You're like locust on a farm.

17:46.690 --> 17:49.359
Whenever you visit, all the food
in my house magically disappears.

17:49.443 --> 17:51.361
You think I can file a claim for all that?

17:51.445 --> 17:53.405
I'll take care of the backyard then.
[chuckles]

17:53.489 --> 17:56.575
Make sure you pull out all the weeds
and spread the cement over there.

17:56.658 --> 17:58.160
- Get a professional for that!
- [Ung] Hey.

17:59.203 --> 18:01.121
The whiskey on my shelf disappeared too.

18:01.205 --> 18:03.791
You know, I happen to be
a cement professional too.

18:03.874 --> 18:04.833
Where should I start?

18:05.959 --> 18:07.044
Hey, Ji-ung.

18:10.964 --> 18:12.424
[scraping]

18:14.301 --> 18:15.219
What's up?

18:15.719 --> 18:16.804
[Ji-ung] Let's film.

18:18.138 --> 18:20.307
- What?
- [Ji-ung] You have to do it.

18:21.725 --> 18:24.061
[groaning sigh]
Please, stop annoying me.

18:25.062 --> 18:28.232
I need to do it. And that means so do you.

18:28.315 --> 18:29.691
What are you on about?

18:30.692 --> 18:33.403
- Did Dad tell you to film me?
- No, that's not it.

18:34.488 --> 18:36.031
You and Yeon-su.

18:37.282 --> 18:39.368
Just like before. A documentary.

18:40.577 --> 18:42.704
[cheeky tense music]

18:50.254 --> 18:52.631
- [Ung] No way.
- Why not?

18:52.714 --> 18:55.300
Are you crazy? Do you really think
I'd film that with her?

18:55.384 --> 18:58.095
He's right. Those two filming
another documentary together?

18:58.178 --> 19:00.889
It'll only take about a month,
and I'll film you myself.

19:00.973 --> 19:03.016
Why are you suddenly
trying to film all that again?

19:04.434 --> 19:08.522
Listen. As you know,
those videos are gaining popularity again.

19:08.605 --> 19:10.649
And we're thinking of filming
a youth documentary

19:10.732 --> 19:12.818
while they're all still trending.
And you're perfect for it.

19:12.901 --> 19:15.070
And most of all,
those videos are gonna be fun.

19:15.154 --> 19:15.988
It's awesome material.

19:16.071 --> 19:17.781
Yeah, very fun.
I'm really pumped for them.

19:17.865 --> 19:20.993
Guys. You know how I broke up with her
all those years ago.

19:21.076 --> 19:22.828
How can you ask me to do that now?

19:22.911 --> 19:24.413
Well, it's already been a long time.

19:24.496 --> 19:26.248
- Unless you still have feelings for her?
- [Ung scoffs]

19:26.331 --> 19:28.125
I don't have any feelings left.
[groans]

19:28.208 --> 19:30.919
I don't even wanna see her again.
Better not to bother anymore.

19:31.003 --> 19:32.921
That means you do have feelings left.

19:34.840 --> 19:35.674
I'm not doing it.

19:38.260 --> 19:41.680
To be honest, I think this is gonna be
a very fun project to work on with you

19:42.181 --> 19:44.349
because of your past relationship.

19:44.433 --> 19:47.060
Why don't you watch those videos again?
There are so many comments,

19:47.144 --> 19:49.396
and you've become
so popular online because of it.

19:49.479 --> 19:51.732
Are you a sociopath?
Are you trying to use me?

19:51.815 --> 19:54.276
And is she even up for it?
I'm sure she isn't.

19:54.359 --> 19:55.903
I already talked to her.

19:57.571 --> 19:58.655
So what…

20:01.700 --> 20:02.701
What did she say?

20:03.285 --> 20:05.537
She started cursing at me,
so I had to back down a bit.

20:06.622 --> 20:08.957
[scoffs]
At least we agree on something.

20:09.708 --> 20:12.002
Anyway, I'm still not doing it.

20:13.170 --> 20:14.922
That's just nonsense, man.

20:17.382 --> 20:18.383
[sighs]

20:18.884 --> 20:20.093
[door closes]

20:20.177 --> 20:22.888
Well, good luck
convincing him any further.

20:22.971 --> 20:24.306
He has an amazing offer,

20:24.389 --> 20:27.601
but he's hesitating because
Yeon-su's gonna be involved in it.

20:27.684 --> 20:28.936
Really?

20:29.019 --> 20:31.480
Then they can work together
and film together too, right?

20:31.563 --> 20:33.273
- [sighs]
- [Eun-ho] But what if they do that,

20:33.857 --> 20:36.360
and Ung starts getting feelings
for her again?

20:40.572 --> 20:43.992
He suddenly asked me
to get him a lot of work recently.

20:44.076 --> 20:45.494
I'm really worried for him.

20:46.286 --> 20:47.204
[inhales]

20:47.287 --> 20:50.707
Maybe his feelings got complicated
after meeting her again like that.

20:52.084 --> 20:54.795
[shudders]
He can't go back to his old habits.

20:54.878 --> 20:56.088
You saw how he was then.

20:56.922 --> 20:58.006
It was crazy.

20:59.049 --> 21:00.425
Can you go through that again?

21:01.551 --> 21:02.761
Don't you remember?

21:05.347 --> 21:07.266
- [Ung screaming]
- [Eun-ho] He was totally crazy

21:07.349 --> 21:09.601
the first few months after they broke up.

21:09.685 --> 21:11.270
5 YEARS AGO
JUNE 20, 2016

21:11.353 --> 21:12.521
- [panting]
- [Eun-ho] Hey, Ung!

21:12.604 --> 21:15.565
[Eun-ho] Come on, man!
Let's go home. Get a grip already!

21:16.817 --> 21:17.901
Eun-ho.

21:19.236 --> 21:21.363
Do you know the thing
that Yeon-su hates the most?

21:22.239 --> 21:23.240
[Eun-ho] What?

21:24.658 --> 21:25.867
Getting drunk

21:27.411 --> 21:29.454
and making a scene late at night.

21:30.080 --> 21:31.456
[Eun-ho] Oh, my gosh.

21:31.540 --> 21:32.874
[screaming]

21:32.958 --> 21:34.668
[Eun-ho] Jeez. You're driving me crazy.

21:34.751 --> 21:35.961
Ung, come on, it's late!

21:36.044 --> 21:36.878
Hey, where are you…

21:36.962 --> 21:40.048
- [Ung screaming]
- Where are you going! Oh, darn it!

21:40.132 --> 21:42.259
[Eun-ho] He did everything
that Yeon-su hated back then…

21:42.342 --> 21:45.304
JUNE 22, 2016

21:45.387 --> 21:47.139
[panting]

21:47.222 --> 21:51.018
Hey, what is it this time?
What do you think you're doing?

21:51.101 --> 21:52.853
Another thing she really hates.

21:52.936 --> 21:55.022
Buying random stuff
while I'm totally plastered.

21:55.105 --> 21:57.482
Why would you nag me
when I'm buying stuff with my own money?

21:58.233 --> 22:00.694
[Eun-ho] …and ran around
like a crazy dog that night.

22:00.777 --> 22:01.945
- [alarm ringing]
- JUNE 23, 2016

22:02.029 --> 22:04.156
[groans]

22:07.117 --> 22:08.201
[groaning]

22:09.369 --> 22:10.329
Ung, wake up.

22:12.873 --> 22:14.750
- I don't wanna.
- You have an exam today.

22:14.833 --> 22:17.252
- Get up already.
- And another thing…

22:17.336 --> 22:18.754
What was that? What did you say?

22:18.837 --> 22:20.714
I'm not going to school

22:21.214 --> 22:23.675
not the day after you drink.

22:24.259 --> 22:25.552
What did you say?

22:25.635 --> 22:28.513
It's the thing
that Yeon-su hates the most.

22:29.431 --> 22:32.517
[Eun-ho] He was acting
like he had completely given up on life.

22:37.230 --> 22:41.234
AUGUST 3, 2016

22:41.318 --> 22:43.320
[soft gentle music]

22:45.572 --> 22:48.116
[Ji-ung] Weren't you the one
who told him about investing in stocks?

22:48.200 --> 22:51.328
[Eun-ho] I read on the internet
that stocks help you get over a breakup.

22:51.411 --> 22:53.580
Stocks during the day
and exercise at night

22:53.663 --> 22:55.040
leaves you no time to think.

22:56.458 --> 22:59.169
[Ji-ung] Oh, well,
I guess it was a bit effective.

23:03.173 --> 23:07.010
He was busy doing part-time jobs
making up for all the money he lost.

23:08.220 --> 23:10.972
- One, two! All right, ready? Here we go!
- [upbeat music plays]

23:11.056 --> 23:13.308
One, two! One, two!

23:14.267 --> 23:16.311
One, two! Two, two!

23:17.062 --> 23:18.980
[Eun-ho] Thanks to me,
he exercised a lot back then,

23:19.064 --> 23:21.358
he managed to stayed healthy.

23:21.441 --> 23:24.194
SEPTEMBER 29, 2016

23:26.279 --> 23:28.281
[whooshing]

23:32.202 --> 23:34.412
[soft somber music]

23:35.372 --> 23:36.790
But, somehow despite that…

23:38.500 --> 23:40.335
he still seemed miserable,

23:40.418 --> 23:42.629
- even when he was so busy.
- [deep sigh]

23:44.422 --> 23:46.758
And after that,
the same patterns repeated several times.

23:46.842 --> 23:47.884
[Eun-ho] Mom.

23:47.968 --> 23:50.262
And then, that period finally began.

23:50.345 --> 23:51.513
He still hasn't come out yet?

23:51.596 --> 23:53.056
[gasps]

23:54.057 --> 23:55.392
[loud knock on door]

23:55.475 --> 23:57.519
Choi Ung. You have to snap out of it.

23:57.602 --> 24:00.147
I'm counting to three,
then I'm just gonna break in.

24:00.230 --> 24:02.983
One, two, three!

24:13.827 --> 24:15.203
[soft sigh]

24:17.497 --> 24:19.958
[soft gentle music]

24:23.295 --> 24:26.506
[Eun-ho] And so if we do put Yeon-su
right next to Ung once again…

24:28.508 --> 24:29.968
wouldn't that be too disastrous?

24:32.137 --> 24:33.930
[sighs deeply]

24:35.182 --> 24:37.225
[soft gentle music]

24:43.815 --> 24:45.942
[Ung] Why does she live
such an exhausting life?

24:46.026 --> 24:48.278
- [chuckles]
- Early birds just get tired earlier.

24:49.654 --> 24:50.947
[Yeon-su] Hurry up!

24:51.031 --> 24:52.365
[Ung] Jeez.

24:52.449 --> 24:55.035
COMMENTS

24:55.118 --> 24:56.369
HE'S LIKE A SQUID

24:56.453 --> 24:57.746
UNG IS SO CUTE

25:00.457 --> 25:01.791
[Ji-ung] You see?

25:02.459 --> 25:04.461
It's nice seeing
compliments like that, right?

25:06.630 --> 25:08.924
Stop pretending to be asleep.
I already saw you.

25:13.345 --> 25:15.013
[sighs]

25:15.889 --> 25:18.225
Anyway, why don't you think about it?

25:19.017 --> 25:22.103
Once you see all the videos,
you might just change your mind.

25:22.854 --> 25:23.772
I know that I did.

25:26.399 --> 25:27.359
And also…

25:30.820 --> 25:32.906
- Never mind.
- [groans]

25:37.285 --> 25:38.620
You know…

25:39.955 --> 25:42.958
I think that Yeon-su hated the idea
more than you did.

25:43.917 --> 25:45.252
[cheeky challenging tune]

25:46.211 --> 25:47.295
I'm just saying.

25:52.592 --> 25:55.011
[cheeky challenging tune]

26:13.238 --> 26:14.906
TRENDING AGAIN
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

26:15.490 --> 26:17.492
[cheeky melody]

26:27.627 --> 26:29.004
TRENDING AGAIN
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

26:31.089 --> 26:33.008
[cheeky melody continues]

26:34.718 --> 26:35.635
[sighs]

26:45.645 --> 26:48.940
SBC SPECIAL DOCUMENTARY
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

26:49.024 --> 26:51.526
Choi Ung skipped study hall
and ran away again.

26:52.110 --> 26:54.070
[Yeon-su] I think he's trying
to ruin his own life.

26:54.154 --> 26:56.114
- Wow, I was so young.
- [Yeon-su] What can I do now?

26:56.197 --> 26:58.825
[gasps]
My skin used to be so elastic.

26:58.908 --> 27:00.076
Hurry up!

27:01.369 --> 27:03.204
[distant chatter on radio]

27:04.456 --> 27:05.582
[sighs]

27:07.000 --> 27:09.669
[Ung] Kook Yeon-su is really good
at exhausting people.

27:10.587 --> 27:12.964
Why does she have to live
such an exhausting life?

27:13.673 --> 27:16.217
I think even early birds
get tired earlier than her.

27:17.385 --> 27:20.722
That's right, I'm still living
an exhausting life right now.

27:21.723 --> 27:22.974
[Ung snoring]

27:23.058 --> 27:25.268
What will he be when he finally grows up?

27:26.061 --> 27:28.021
We can sleep all we want when we're dead.

27:28.521 --> 27:31.691
I'm sure he'll be lazy
for his entire life. You can count on it.

27:33.276 --> 27:36.196
[Yeon-su] But then he became
a famous artist after all.

27:38.239 --> 27:40.283
Life really is unfair sometimes.

27:46.831 --> 27:48.833
[chuckles softly]

27:49.334 --> 27:51.878
["Drawer" by 10CM playing]

28:01.221 --> 28:02.764
[chuckles softly]

28:10.522 --> 28:11.356
Oh?

28:12.982 --> 28:15.110
IT'S BEEN TEN YEARS ALREADY
I WONDER WHAT THEY'RE UP TO

28:15.193 --> 28:18.363
THIS IS WHAT BEING YOUNG IS ALL ABOUT

28:18.446 --> 28:21.199
THEY'RE SO YOUNG AND INNOCENT
LIKE SUMMERTIME

28:21.783 --> 28:23.201
[Ung] I thought you were a ghost!

28:27.372 --> 28:30.750
[Ung and Yeon-su] "I guess you might say
this is what being young is all about."

28:31.251 --> 28:34.087
"They're so young and innocent,
like summertime."

28:34.170 --> 28:36.881
"It's something only the youth can have."

28:37.590 --> 28:39.342
[water gushing]

28:39.426 --> 28:41.761
["Drawer" by 10CM continues]

28:44.597 --> 28:45.682
Sorry.

28:48.560 --> 28:49.853
Hey! Hey!

28:50.687 --> 28:52.856
- [chuckling]
- No! I said I'm sorry!

28:52.939 --> 28:53.982
[chuckles]
Sorry!

28:54.065 --> 28:55.108
Hey.

28:56.484 --> 28:58.570
[both laughing]

29:01.030 --> 29:02.866
Hey, you! No running in the halls.

29:06.035 --> 29:07.662
Hey!

29:08.621 --> 29:10.874
Kook Yeon-su! You psycho!

29:12.667 --> 29:15.420
["Drawer" by 10CM playing]

29:21.092 --> 29:24.095
Oh, damn it.
Why did Ji-ung have to bring it up again?

29:25.430 --> 29:26.973
- [groans]
- [thuds]

29:27.056 --> 29:28.308
[groans in pain]

29:31.478 --> 29:34.606
[Yeon-su] I won't even see him again.
That's all right, I guess.

29:36.941 --> 29:38.318
[tapping keys]

29:41.780 --> 29:44.657
ARTIST NU-A

29:45.241 --> 29:46.743
But the problem is…

29:53.041 --> 29:54.542
[soft whirring]

29:56.127 --> 29:58.546
[awkward music]

30:02.342 --> 30:03.676
[engine starting]

30:06.095 --> 30:08.097
[awkward music continues]

30:11.226 --> 30:12.685
I never once ran into him

30:12.769 --> 30:15.438
during the past five years,
but then on that day…

30:17.148 --> 30:19.150
[engine humming]

30:22.904 --> 30:24.531
[yelps in surprise]

30:24.614 --> 30:26.783
- [crashing]
- [woman] Oh, my goodness.

30:27.784 --> 30:29.077
[groans in pain]

30:29.160 --> 30:31.246
[grunts, pants]

30:34.165 --> 30:36.501
[awkward music]

30:43.508 --> 30:44.551
[Ung] But, then…

30:45.677 --> 30:48.221
we keep running into each other.
It was so strange.

30:51.182 --> 30:52.100
[groans]

31:00.149 --> 31:02.360
["Squabble" by Ha Sung Woon playing]

31:08.366 --> 31:10.827
Oh. Wait. I left my crutch!

31:11.327 --> 31:13.121
- Just wait a minute, sir.
- [brake squeals]

31:18.918 --> 31:20.920
Are you fucking kidding me?

31:21.504 --> 31:23.673
[Yeon-su] Maybe it could happen
once or twice.

31:25.967 --> 31:26.801
[gasps]

31:28.428 --> 31:29.470
[Ung] Excuse me.

31:32.765 --> 31:34.601
[Ung] How is this even possible?

31:35.727 --> 31:37.770
["Squabble" by Ha Sung Woon continues]

31:39.439 --> 31:40.815
[bag tears]

31:43.568 --> 31:44.944
[long sigh]

31:45.612 --> 31:47.196
Why the hell is this happening?

31:49.908 --> 31:51.993
["Squabble" by Ha Sung Woon playing]

31:52.076 --> 31:53.161
[scoffs]

31:56.998 --> 31:59.375
- [Ung] Oh.
- [stifled chuckle]

32:02.337 --> 32:04.589
[Ung] Why in the world
is this happening to me?

32:06.424 --> 32:07.300
[Ung sighs]

32:09.844 --> 32:12.013
The paper bags here, they're really so…

32:12.639 --> 32:15.224
[objects rattle]

32:18.478 --> 32:20.647
Hey, are you following me around?

32:20.730 --> 32:22.398
Why would you think something like that?

32:22.482 --> 32:24.233
Then what are you doing here
in my neighborhood, huh?

32:24.317 --> 32:26.444
Hey, this is near my house too, you know.

32:26.527 --> 32:28.112
But didn't you move?

32:28.196 --> 32:30.448
So? Do you even know where I live now?

32:34.243 --> 32:36.037
Hey. Does this even make sense?

32:36.120 --> 32:38.873
We never ran into each other
for the past five years.

32:38.957 --> 32:40.833
If it bothers you, then go somewhere else.

32:41.334 --> 32:42.502
What's that?

32:42.585 --> 32:44.504
[scoffs]
You're the one who seems bothered.

32:44.587 --> 32:45.797
Maybe you should go somewhere else.

32:45.880 --> 32:48.341
[Yeon-su] And he's still
as childish as he ever was back then.

32:48.424 --> 32:50.468
What? Not me, why would I?

32:50.551 --> 32:53.554
You mean nothing to me.
Why the heck should I be bothered?

32:53.638 --> 32:57.058
[Ung] How in the world is she this skilled
at annoying the hell out of me?

32:57.141 --> 32:58.267
[groans]

32:58.351 --> 33:01.980
You. You're lingering around me
because of that project, aren't you?

33:02.063 --> 33:03.898
And you're hoping
I'll change my mind about it.

33:03.982 --> 33:07.235
Oh, that? You don't need
to worry about it anymore.

33:07.318 --> 33:09.195
We're getting another artist instead.

33:09.988 --> 33:10.863
What? Who?

33:10.947 --> 33:13.032
There's this artist named Nu-a
who's pretty popular--

33:13.116 --> 33:14.450
[chuckles]

33:14.534 --> 33:17.245
Hey, Nu-a's just a total knockoff.

33:17.328 --> 33:19.789
You know he's always just
copying my drawing style.

33:19.872 --> 33:23.793
Well, I'm sure the public will find out
who's copying who very soon, I think.

33:23.876 --> 33:24.794
In fact,

33:24.877 --> 33:27.338
Nu-a's art is much better than yours.

33:27.922 --> 33:29.757
Hey, come on, don't say that.

33:30.341 --> 33:32.468
Hey, where are you going?
I'm not done here.

33:32.552 --> 33:36.139
Well, you seem to be bothered by me,
so I'm doing my best to avoid you.

33:36.222 --> 33:37.056
Hey, I'm not.

33:37.140 --> 33:40.768
And you really shouldn't work with Nu-a,
all right? You'll regret it later on.

33:40.852 --> 33:42.603
Just find some other artist to work with.

33:43.563 --> 33:45.732
- Hey, just listen to me. Hey!
- [thuds]

33:46.232 --> 33:48.401
Oh, oops. My bad.

33:48.484 --> 33:50.695
It went all the way over there.
So go get it.

33:51.571 --> 33:54.323
- Hey, Kook Yeon-su!
- I can be childish too, you know.

33:54.407 --> 33:56.159
[Yeon-su] I should've done this earlier.

33:56.242 --> 33:57.285
Feels great.

34:00.121 --> 34:02.623
- What?
- It was supposed to be Go-oh.

34:02.707 --> 34:06.419
He said he'll cancel the contract
if you're working with Nu-a instead.

34:08.421 --> 34:09.505
You said you found Go-oh.

34:09.589 --> 34:11.507
Why are you changing
the artist all of a sudden?

34:11.591 --> 34:12.675
[awkward groan]

34:13.426 --> 34:15.803
Well, I know that Nu-a is also
a popular artist these days.

34:16.387 --> 34:18.389
And I think the art style
suits Soen Shop very well.

34:18.473 --> 34:20.308
And Nu-a seemed
to want to work with us too.

34:20.391 --> 34:23.061
Yes, I know, but he said
he only wants Go-oh.

34:23.561 --> 34:24.896
Why? Did he ask for too much money?

34:24.979 --> 34:26.647
- [I-hun] Was his price too steep?
- [sighs]

34:26.731 --> 34:28.733
Well, you see, it's…

34:28.816 --> 34:31.652
Yeon-su. The plan was going well already.
What's going on?

34:31.736 --> 34:34.989
You know how important
this project is for our company, right?

34:35.073 --> 34:36.866
Everyone is relying on you for this.

34:36.949 --> 34:38.826
[sighs deeply]

34:40.661 --> 34:44.123
Darn it. Well,
if he wants more than our budget,

34:44.207 --> 34:45.917
then write up a new estimate for him.

34:46.000 --> 34:47.835
I'll try to make it work,
but just get it done.

34:49.420 --> 34:50.505
[sighs]

35:08.773 --> 35:10.733
[sighs]

35:11.442 --> 35:14.070
[Yeon-su] Why does everything
have to be messed up like this?

35:14.570 --> 35:17.031
[gentle music]

35:17.115 --> 35:19.033
[Yeon-su groaning]

35:20.159 --> 35:24.205
Ever since Choi Ung popped up again,
things have been going downhill.

35:26.165 --> 35:27.667
[phone buzzing]

35:29.544 --> 35:30.670
Goodbye, sir.

35:30.753 --> 35:32.338
Mm. All right. Take care.

35:32.421 --> 35:33.965
[distant telephone rings]

35:35.216 --> 35:37.552
[sighs deeply]
Where is this jerk?

35:37.635 --> 35:38.803
I haven't seen him all day.

35:38.886 --> 35:41.347
Where in the world did that guy
run off to anyway?

35:41.430 --> 35:44.016
He said he's trying to cast
the people from the documentary.

35:45.351 --> 35:46.310
Is that so?

35:46.394 --> 35:47.895
Well, did he have any luck?

35:48.813 --> 35:50.398
He never reports his progress to me.

35:51.524 --> 35:53.943
He never fails
when he sets his mind on something.

35:54.026 --> 35:55.194
[Dong-il] I guess.

35:55.695 --> 35:56.988
That's why I can't scold him.

35:57.947 --> 35:59.073
But why did he…

36:00.199 --> 36:03.411
suddenly decide to do the documentary
in the first place?

36:03.494 --> 36:06.205
He spent days browsing through old videos.

36:06.289 --> 36:08.374
I guess he got interested
after doing that.

36:09.500 --> 36:10.626
He watched everything?

36:12.378 --> 36:13.671
[chuckles]

36:15.173 --> 36:16.340
Hey, you know what?

36:17.049 --> 36:18.259
I did a good job of filming.

36:18.342 --> 36:21.137
There are so many fun
behind the scene cuts on those clips.

36:22.305 --> 36:26.017
So you say he watched everything, huh?
That's kind of adorable.

36:26.100 --> 36:28.269
Come to think of it,
I hadn't thought of it before,

36:28.352 --> 36:30.646
Ji-ung was pretty cute
when he was in high school.

36:31.439 --> 36:32.940
I remember when he appeared on the screen,

36:33.649 --> 36:35.109
I recall he would freeze.

36:35.943 --> 36:37.403
[chuckles]

36:37.486 --> 36:41.407
By the way, why do you always
ask me about Ji-ung anyway?

36:42.533 --> 36:43.576
What?

36:43.659 --> 36:46.495
Everyone keeps asking me
about Ji-ung, not just you.

36:46.579 --> 36:48.956
Oh. Well, I mean…

36:51.083 --> 36:52.627
Because you know the most about him.

36:52.710 --> 36:54.503
- Don't you?
- What?

36:54.587 --> 36:57.465
Everyone always asks you first
when they're looking for Ji-ung.

36:57.548 --> 36:59.383
Didn't you notice that happening?

37:01.469 --> 37:03.387
- [Chae-ran] Why though?
- It's obvious.

37:07.183 --> 37:10.186
[cheeky tense music]

37:22.990 --> 37:25.493
Should I tell you
what Ji-ung was like in high school?

37:26.535 --> 37:29.580
- Well, if you're not curious…
- You can tell me if you're bored instead.

37:31.958 --> 37:33.292
[Dong-il clears throat]

37:34.919 --> 37:35.962
[sighs]

37:36.754 --> 37:38.214
Looking at Ji-ung…

37:41.425 --> 37:44.762
always reminds me
of my old high school days.

37:44.845 --> 37:47.265
So I have to tell you
about my high school days first.

37:47.348 --> 37:50.434
Why did Ms. Kook suddenly
get off work so early?

37:50.518 --> 37:53.354
She probably went to Go-oh
to talk about our new project.

37:53.437 --> 37:55.481
Well, at least,
we got to get off work early.

37:55.564 --> 37:57.024
Well then, you guys wanna get drinks?

37:57.108 --> 37:59.777
Oh, no. I'm on a diet right now. Mm.

38:00.736 --> 38:01.737
What?

38:03.239 --> 38:05.783
No way. hey, isn't that Ms. Kook?

38:06.575 --> 38:07.868
Oh!

38:09.578 --> 38:12.290
[Myeong-ho] Don't tell me
she got off early to go on a date?

38:12.373 --> 38:15.042
Wow, they look
so good together, don't they?

38:15.126 --> 38:17.169
[Ye-in] I can't believe
she's actually dating.

38:17.253 --> 38:18.546
Wait, there's no way.

38:19.255 --> 38:21.841
- That's impossible.
- What's so impossible about it?

38:22.675 --> 38:23.801
To be honest,

38:24.510 --> 38:27.471
- I was shipping her with someone else.
- What do you mean by that?

38:27.555 --> 38:30.308
Is she going somewhere?
What's going on? Come on, tell us.

38:30.391 --> 38:33.102
[groans]
No, that's not what I meant, you guys.

38:33.185 --> 38:35.479
I mean, I thought that
she would end up dating

38:36.063 --> 38:37.857
Mr. Jang over anybody else.

38:37.940 --> 38:39.525
What? Her and Mr. Jang?

38:39.608 --> 38:40.901
What are you trying to say?

38:40.985 --> 38:42.862
[chuckles]
I have a bit of a sixth sense

38:42.945 --> 38:44.780
when it comes
to stuff like this, you know.

38:44.864 --> 38:47.825
Something's going on
between Ms. Kook and Mr. Jang.

38:47.908 --> 38:50.202
It's so juicy, I can almost smell it.

38:50.286 --> 38:52.079
And they do look good together,
don't they?

38:52.163 --> 38:53.456
Come on, how can you say that?

38:53.539 --> 38:54.957
They've always been
at each other's throats.

38:55.041 --> 38:57.209
But that's how romance begins,
you crazy fools.

38:57.293 --> 38:58.878
- Oh, you're so clueless.
- No, I'm not.

38:58.961 --> 39:00.838
Wait a sec, haven't you been proven wrong?

39:00.921 --> 39:02.340
We just saw her with that guy.

39:02.840 --> 39:05.092
Oh, well, I don't think
we can know for sure yet.

39:05.593 --> 39:06.844
I have to keep watching them.

39:06.927 --> 39:09.180
Then how about we discuss all that

39:09.263 --> 39:12.058
over some thin pork belly
on a hot grill then?

39:12.141 --> 39:14.852
Didn't you hear what I said?
I'm on a diet right now.

39:14.935 --> 39:18.147
Didn't you hear what I said?
Thin pork belly on a hot grill.

39:18.230 --> 39:19.523
[groans]

39:20.649 --> 39:22.485
Well, I guess thin slices are okay.

39:22.568 --> 39:23.444
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

39:23.527 --> 39:26.572
- Come on.
- [music ends]

39:28.657 --> 39:30.743
I think you're just
wasting your time with this.

39:30.826 --> 39:32.161
I told you I won't do it.

39:32.244 --> 39:33.746
Still, you have to give me a reason.

39:33.829 --> 39:35.081
Don't you know already?

39:35.164 --> 39:37.124
It's Choi Ung.
Why would I do any of that with him?

39:37.708 --> 39:40.461
Well, why not?
There's nothing between you two anyway.

39:41.045 --> 39:42.880
You don't have
lingering feelings left, do you?

39:43.672 --> 39:45.466
Did you come here
just to make jokes with me?

39:45.549 --> 39:48.427
That childish method won't work on me.
So try that on Choi Ung.

39:48.511 --> 39:49.345
[scoffs]

39:50.596 --> 39:53.849
- I knew it wouldn't work.
- Then why did you come all the way here?

39:53.933 --> 39:55.851
It's still my job
to get you on board, that's why.

39:56.602 --> 39:58.062
If that method doesn't work,

39:59.063 --> 40:00.272
I'll have to use another approach.

40:00.856 --> 40:02.566
Fine. I'm sure I won't change my mind,

40:02.650 --> 40:05.069
but I'll listen
to what you have to say. Go on then.

40:10.199 --> 40:11.492
Why do you think

40:11.575 --> 40:14.745
people decide to star in a documentary
when it's all about themselves?

40:16.789 --> 40:18.707
Oh. Well…

40:19.333 --> 40:21.210
To promote their businesses, or maybe…

40:21.293 --> 40:24.130
Oh, yeah? I'm sure most of them
don't have businesses to promote.

40:25.339 --> 40:26.757
For the pay, then.

40:26.841 --> 40:29.343
You get paid for them.
That's why I did it back then.

40:29.427 --> 40:31.262
Then you should know
it's not that huge of a sum, right?

40:31.345 --> 40:33.305
Are you telling me to come up
with a reason?

40:33.806 --> 40:35.599
I'm always honest when I'm casting people.

40:35.683 --> 40:38.519
"There's only one thing
we can give to you.

40:38.602 --> 40:40.146
But we know it'll be worth it.

40:41.564 --> 40:44.900
We are recording
a fraction of your life just for you."

40:47.236 --> 40:50.448
When I say this, most people
seem to think that it's no big deal

40:50.531 --> 40:52.450
and what I do
doesn't really matter at all.

40:52.533 --> 40:53.534
But then…

40:54.952 --> 40:56.537
after we finish filming them,

40:56.620 --> 40:58.414
and when they finally
see the video themselves,

40:58.497 --> 41:00.624
then they realize what it really meant.

41:02.251 --> 41:03.461
[Ji-ung] They get to realize

41:03.544 --> 41:07.673
how precious it is to be able to
capture and store a moment in their lives.

41:09.258 --> 41:12.219
And that's why it's actually easier for me
to convince you specifically

41:12.303 --> 41:14.638
to film an interview
than it is with others.

41:16.807 --> 41:18.726
You've had those records before, right?

41:20.769 --> 41:22.605
Then you'll know what will fit best.

41:22.688 --> 41:25.232
You have a part of the summer
when you were still 19.

41:25.316 --> 41:26.609
Now tell me the truth.

41:26.692 --> 41:28.277
Does that really mean nothing to you?

41:29.153 --> 41:31.113
[inhales, hums]

41:32.781 --> 41:33.824
I guess…

41:34.742 --> 41:36.160
Did you see the other videos?

41:37.995 --> 41:38.871
No.

41:38.954 --> 41:41.290
You and Ung are not so different
from each other, you know?

41:42.166 --> 41:44.919
[Ji-ung] Why are you both
so hesitant to watch those videos?

41:45.711 --> 41:47.296
To be honest, way back then

41:47.880 --> 41:49.965
I really thought
that all of this meant nothing.

41:50.049 --> 41:52.510
But when I looked through the videos,
I had a realization

41:52.593 --> 41:54.803
you and Ung, the two of you

41:54.887 --> 41:57.264
are the most suited
for our youth special documentary.

41:57.848 --> 42:00.226
[soft gentle music]

42:01.227 --> 42:02.520
You're good with words, Ji-ung.

42:04.230 --> 42:05.231
Respect.

42:06.065 --> 42:08.609
But sorry, you've failed to convince me.
So I won't do it.

42:13.239 --> 42:14.156
[slurps]

42:16.116 --> 42:17.034
Oh, well.

42:18.619 --> 42:19.620
What?

42:22.081 --> 42:24.083
- Is that it?
- [soft sigh]

42:24.166 --> 42:25.960
I have never failed at casting people.

42:27.545 --> 42:29.380
That means I have another plan.

42:30.381 --> 42:33.133
- [mischievous music]
- That makes me feel uneasy.

42:34.343 --> 42:37.846
Will you tell me
if I ask you what you're doing?

42:39.473 --> 42:40.349
[inhales]

42:41.517 --> 42:43.018
It's about Ung…

42:43.102 --> 42:45.104
[mischievous music continues]

42:47.106 --> 42:48.732
I can't let her work with Nu-a.

42:48.816 --> 42:51.652
There, you see? You should have
thanked her and accepted her offer

42:51.735 --> 42:54.405
when she wanted to work with you then.
What were you thinking, huh?

42:54.488 --> 42:56.365
Why would I thank you? I'm not crazy.

42:56.448 --> 42:59.577
Grown-ups should know how to keep
their personal life separate from work.

43:00.119 --> 43:03.289
Everyone's nagging me about that
as if everyone can do it so well.

43:03.372 --> 43:06.208
Wow, you're such a loser. Unbelievable.

43:07.334 --> 43:09.086
Ung, be honest with me.

43:09.169 --> 43:11.630
You want Yeon-su to come
and beg you to work with her, don't you?

43:11.714 --> 43:13.799
You're doing this
because you wanna see her begging you,

43:13.882 --> 43:16.552
even if this is all
just because of work, am I right?

43:16.635 --> 43:18.429
[gulps, sighs]

43:18.512 --> 43:20.681
- She'll never do that.
- See? That's what I mean!

43:20.764 --> 43:23.225
If you know that,
why are you even doing all of this?

43:23.309 --> 43:26.020
Honestly, you sound like the one
picking fights with her.

43:26.604 --> 43:28.105
It's so annoying, man.

43:28.188 --> 43:30.941
Pretending she doesn't feel anything,
that she doesn't care.

43:31.025 --> 43:32.568
[Yeon-su] What? Not me, why would I?

43:32.651 --> 43:35.029
You mean nothing to me.
Why the heck should I be bothered?

43:35.112 --> 43:36.822
She was always like that.

43:36.905 --> 43:39.033
Oh, that? You don't need
to worry about it anymore.

43:39.116 --> 43:40.534
We're getting another artist instead.

43:40.618 --> 43:43.245
There's this artist named Nu-a
who's pretty popular…

43:43.329 --> 43:45.497
She's so selfish
and always so full of herself.

43:45.581 --> 43:46.832
And yet, she still won.

43:48.459 --> 43:50.961
Just go and say that you agree,
and you'll do the project.

43:51.045 --> 43:54.214
If you wanna do it, of course they still
have to decide to do it with you or not.

43:54.298 --> 43:57.092
Hey, wait a second, why would I ever
do something that would help her?

43:57.635 --> 43:59.887
I should be doing stuff
that she hates instead.

44:01.847 --> 44:03.265
[groans]

44:04.892 --> 44:07.102
[intense music]

44:08.812 --> 44:10.648
[Ung] I just had an idea.

44:12.024 --> 44:14.026
[intense music continues]

44:21.533 --> 44:23.994
[Eun-ho] What's that face?
I have a bad feeling about this.

44:25.579 --> 44:26.789
That's right.

44:27.373 --> 44:30.042
I should be doing stuff that she hates.

44:30.125 --> 44:32.795
[Ung] That'll be a great way
to win over Kook Yeon-su.

44:34.421 --> 44:36.924
Uh, I don't know what you're thinking,
but I'm gonna stop you right there.

44:37.007 --> 44:37.966
Hey, Eun-ho.

44:39.134 --> 44:40.886
I have some work for you to do.

44:40.969 --> 44:42.805
What? I already spread all that cement.

44:43.305 --> 44:45.849
Not that. I meant,
I want you to work as my manager.

44:45.933 --> 44:48.018
Your what? NJ?

44:49.144 --> 44:52.064
Is this work for NJ?
Can I really look forward to it this time?

44:53.023 --> 44:56.151
- [cheerful music]
- [chuckles]

45:00.572 --> 45:03.283
[Ung] Why didn't I think of this before?

45:05.327 --> 45:06.620
[music stops]

45:09.123 --> 45:09.957
[beeps]

45:15.546 --> 45:16.588
[chimes]

45:23.262 --> 45:24.388
[sighs]

45:26.849 --> 45:30.602
[exhales]
He's a total player. I'm sure of it.

45:30.686 --> 45:32.062
[sighs]

45:35.315 --> 45:38.110
[NJ] Why do guys always say
that they'll contact you, but never do so?

45:38.694 --> 45:41.530
He said he would,
he said that he would contact me first

45:41.613 --> 45:43.449
so that I could even contact him.

45:43.532 --> 45:46.034
But it's been days already,
and he still hasn't contacted me.

45:46.118 --> 45:49.413
Why in the world is he acting like this?
He even told me he was my fan…

45:49.496 --> 45:50.622
[sighs]

45:53.000 --> 45:55.085
He said he liked me when we first met.

45:55.169 --> 45:58.213
But why isn't he contacting me?
What's going on?

45:59.840 --> 46:00.716
[phone beeping]

46:01.717 --> 46:03.677
[woman 1] Don't you know the answer?
He's not into you.

46:03.760 --> 46:05.387
[woman 2] I don't think
he's interested in you.

46:05.471 --> 46:07.473
[woman 3] He's keeping you
on the hook, that's all.

46:07.556 --> 46:09.683
[woman 4] He could just be
pretty cautious maybe.

46:12.978 --> 46:14.188
[content sigh]

46:24.740 --> 46:26.992
[plotting music]

46:28.869 --> 46:32.915
CHOI UNG

46:41.465 --> 46:43.091
Hi. My name is Gu Eun-ho.

46:45.177 --> 46:47.179
GU EUN-HO

46:47.262 --> 46:50.474
QUEENJ_EUNHOW

46:50.557 --> 46:53.268
[plotting music continues]

46:55.854 --> 46:57.147
[chuckles softly]

46:59.316 --> 47:00.484
STAY HEALTHY

47:04.780 --> 47:07.157
WENT DRINKING WITH UNG

47:07.241 --> 47:09.034
[annoyed scoff]
He's drinking and having fun,

47:09.618 --> 47:12.037
but not making the effort
to even try calling me.

47:15.832 --> 47:16.667
No, I can't.

47:16.750 --> 47:19.002
I can't press "like" on
a non-celebrity's account.

47:21.213 --> 47:22.130
[sighs]

47:27.636 --> 47:29.054
[sighs]

47:29.137 --> 47:31.431
[gentle comforting music]

47:46.071 --> 47:48.865
[Ung] All right, all right, man, I get it.

47:48.949 --> 47:52.828
Yeah. Yes, I'm totally safe, man. Okay?

47:53.495 --> 47:55.539
Yeah, and I'm almost home!

47:55.622 --> 47:56.540
Yeah.

47:57.541 --> 47:58.625
All right.

47:58.709 --> 47:59.710
[phone chimes]

48:01.378 --> 48:03.672
Gosh, it sure has been a while.

48:03.755 --> 48:05.882
[sighs, inhales]

48:09.970 --> 48:11.263
Wait a sec.

48:19.646 --> 48:20.856
I knew it.

48:21.773 --> 48:23.442
It's Kook Yeon-su again.

48:23.525 --> 48:25.277
[deep sigh]

48:25.360 --> 48:27.487
Did everyone else
in the neighborhood disappear?

48:27.571 --> 48:28.947
Why is it always her?

48:38.123 --> 48:39.082
Were you drinking again?

48:42.919 --> 48:44.921
["Maybe If" by BIBI playing]

48:50.385 --> 48:51.720
Okay. Just go back home already.

48:52.804 --> 48:55.265
[Ung] Ten reasons why I hate Kook Yeon-su.

48:56.183 --> 48:58.310
Am I the easiest thing to throw away

48:59.186 --> 49:00.270
of all the things you have?

49:02.314 --> 49:03.315
No.

49:04.358 --> 49:05.859
But you're the only one…

49:07.027 --> 49:08.236
that I can get rid of.

49:11.740 --> 49:12.991
What's the reason?

49:16.244 --> 49:17.704
[louder]
What's your reason?

49:19.081 --> 49:20.916
[Ung shouting mentally]
Why do we have to break up?

49:20.999 --> 49:24.711
♪ It never seems to disappear ♪

49:24.795 --> 49:28.173
["Maybe If" by BIBI continues]

49:47.776 --> 49:50.070
["Maybe If" by BIBI continues]

50:00.747 --> 50:02.791
[Ung] The tenth and the last reason

50:03.792 --> 50:08.338
is because she erased me
from her life so easily.

50:20.767 --> 50:21.935
[all chuckling]

50:22.436 --> 50:23.770
Good morning, everyone.

50:23.854 --> 50:25.480
- Good morning.
- Oh, good morning, Ms. Kook!

50:26.273 --> 50:28.066
[Yeon-su] You all seem
to be in a good mood.

50:28.150 --> 50:30.902
Well, you see, huh,
you gave us an amazing present,

50:30.986 --> 50:32.112
of course, we'd be happy.

50:32.195 --> 50:33.905
- What are you talking about?
- Oh, come on, now.

50:33.989 --> 50:36.867
Didn't you stay quiet all this time
just to surprise us?

50:36.950 --> 50:38.285
I don't know what you're talking about.

50:38.368 --> 50:40.579
[Myeong-ho] Someone from
Go-oh's agency dropped by here.

50:40.662 --> 50:43.248
And we heard that
you were friends with Go-oh.

50:43.331 --> 50:45.292
So why didn't you tell us about it?

50:45.375 --> 50:47.669
Wait. Who dropped by earlier?

50:47.753 --> 50:51.047
His manager came to say
he'll work on the Soen Shop project.

50:51.715 --> 50:53.425
Choi Ung, uh, no, I mean,

50:54.009 --> 50:55.761
Go-oh really said
that he'd do it, for real?

50:55.844 --> 50:59.222
Yes. He said that he'd do it
because you were going to help him

50:59.306 --> 51:00.766
with something as well.

51:01.892 --> 51:04.227
- He said I would?
- "I would"?

51:04.311 --> 51:05.687
[chuckling]

51:05.771 --> 51:06.980
Come on, quit playing.

51:07.481 --> 51:10.275
[I-hun] Who knew you would have
such connections, Yeon-su?

51:10.358 --> 51:12.861
I already told Soen Shop
about the good news too.

51:13.570 --> 51:16.239
[Yeon-su] No way. No, that's impossible.

51:16.323 --> 51:19.910
I… could you please excuse me?
I need to meet someone.

51:19.993 --> 51:21.369
I'll be back in a bit.

51:21.953 --> 51:22.871
What's up?

51:22.954 --> 51:24.664
[music fades]

51:31.379 --> 51:33.757
[Eun-ho] Why did you send me
to get the contract so early?

51:33.840 --> 51:35.217
I thought it was about NJ.

51:36.343 --> 51:37.719
You did as I told you?

51:37.803 --> 51:38.720
Yes.

51:39.387 --> 51:40.806
And did you meet Yeon-su?

51:40.889 --> 51:42.307
No, she wasn't there.

51:43.183 --> 51:44.559
Is that so?

51:46.061 --> 51:47.938
It's going to get noisy here soon.

51:48.605 --> 51:49.773
I suggest you stay away.

51:50.607 --> 51:51.817
Why?

51:51.900 --> 51:54.069
It's going to be a mess here soon.

51:55.612 --> 51:56.863
Hmm?

51:56.947 --> 52:01.076
One, ten, hundred, thousand… 17,867?

52:01.159 --> 52:06.039
Why did 17,867 people like
the photo I posted of us eating meat?

52:06.122 --> 52:07.040
What are you talking about?

52:13.839 --> 52:15.257
[gasps dramatically]

52:16.842 --> 52:18.009
Oh, come on.

52:19.302 --> 52:20.178
NJ.

52:21.096 --> 52:23.682
NJ liked my photo of us eating!

52:23.765 --> 52:25.058
What?

52:26.059 --> 52:27.727
Look.
[gasps]

52:27.811 --> 52:28.895
NJ!

52:28.979 --> 52:30.355
[doorbell ringing]

52:30.438 --> 52:32.023
[chuckles happily]

52:32.107 --> 52:33.900
[Eun-ho] I can't believe
NJ liked my photo!

52:34.693 --> 52:36.987
Oh, God, NJ really liked my photo!

52:37.070 --> 52:38.613
[chuckles happily]

52:39.155 --> 52:40.407
[sighs]

52:40.490 --> 52:41.950
[Ji-ung] So about Ung…

52:43.076 --> 52:44.494
When we were about nine,

52:44.578 --> 52:46.913
I always teased him
and ran away back in those days.

52:47.622 --> 52:48.623
So what about it?

52:48.707 --> 52:51.084
I think he just wanted to get back at me.

52:51.167 --> 52:53.628
[Ji-ung] One day, he brought
some shaved ice to eat together.

52:54.254 --> 52:55.922
So I gladly ate it up.

52:56.006 --> 52:59.676
Even if I had a terrible allergy
to the peaches added to it.

53:00.468 --> 53:02.804
[Yeon-su] But wait,
isn't he allergic to them as well?

53:02.888 --> 53:04.389
[chuckles]
That crazy jerk.

53:04.472 --> 53:07.183
You know, he gladly ate peaches
with me just to get revenge.

53:07.267 --> 53:09.227
[sighs]
Unbelievable.

53:09.311 --> 53:10.770
So then what happened to you guys?

53:11.354 --> 53:14.524
We both got sent
to the emergency room with puffy faces,

53:14.608 --> 53:18.862
and he even smirked at me
from the bed right across mine.

53:19.487 --> 53:21.740
So that's when I decided
to stop bullying him.

53:22.574 --> 53:24.492
So why are you telling me all of this?

53:25.869 --> 53:30.498
Well, Choi Ung, um, he's the type
who's willing to endure his own pain,

53:30.582 --> 53:33.501
if it means he can make others suffer
just as badly, if not worse.

53:33.585 --> 53:37.130
And I'm sure that
you'll realize what I mean soon.

53:38.590 --> 53:40.133
[Yeon-su] No, there's no way.

53:40.216 --> 53:42.761
Would Choi Ung
really be that crazy like he said?

53:45.055 --> 53:47.432
Well, that's what I thought at first,

53:47.515 --> 53:50.018
but then seeing his face
all but confirmed it.

53:50.101 --> 53:51.645
[sighs]

53:51.728 --> 53:52.979
He really is crazy.

53:54.564 --> 53:56.066
What do you mean?

53:57.317 --> 53:59.611
Did you agree to work
on our project just because…

54:00.195 --> 54:02.447
Hmm. Because you'll be helping me too.

54:04.115 --> 54:06.284
And by helping you, do you mean that…

54:06.368 --> 54:09.037
I wanna film that documentary with you.

54:09.120 --> 54:10.121
Again.

54:10.205 --> 54:12.707
[Ung] This may not be different
from when I ate those peaches.

54:12.791 --> 54:14.668
I guess we can
chalk that up to my condition.

54:14.751 --> 54:15.835
Let's film it together.

54:16.503 --> 54:19.005
The documentary I mean. Just for a month.

54:21.341 --> 54:22.509
That's it.

54:24.219 --> 54:25.303
Choi Ung!

54:26.763 --> 54:28.723
[Ung] If Kook Yeon-su hates it this much,

54:29.349 --> 54:31.017
then I can take it.

54:33.144 --> 54:34.729
[Ung sighs contently]

54:38.316 --> 54:39.234
EPILOGUE

54:39.317 --> 54:40.860
[chuckles]

54:40.944 --> 54:42.737
This is so ridiculous.

54:43.321 --> 54:45.281
Does he still really hate me that much?

54:46.408 --> 54:49.953
Hmm. Well, I guess for me…

54:50.662 --> 54:51.913
I don't really care.

54:53.039 --> 54:55.583
You know, I'd like to think
I'm kind of a cool person.

54:55.667 --> 54:57.585
I don't really
hold grudges against people.

54:57.669 --> 54:58.545
I mean it.

55:00.922 --> 55:03.633
FIVE YEARS AGO
AFTER THE BREAKUP

55:03.717 --> 55:04.801
[sighs]

55:06.469 --> 55:08.722
[indistinct chatter]

55:19.441 --> 55:21.818
[gentle music]

55:26.614 --> 55:28.408
- Here, please enjoy.
- Thank you so much.

55:28.491 --> 55:30.994
- Oh, you can leave that here instead.
- Yeah, thank you.

55:32.370 --> 55:34.080
- [doorbell tingling]
- Oh.

55:34.164 --> 55:35.582
[Yeon-su] Hi, welcome.

55:35.665 --> 55:37.709
- [woman] Yeah, I'd like to order this.
- [Yeon-su] Yes.

55:39.002 --> 55:41.004
[gentle music continues]

55:42.714 --> 55:44.758
[student chatter]

55:48.595 --> 55:50.430
If you have something to say,

55:50.513 --> 55:52.307
stop staring at me and just say it.

55:52.390 --> 55:54.642
[indistinct chatter]

55:56.853 --> 55:58.354
Are you really feeling okay?

56:00.732 --> 56:02.609
- What's that?
- Sorry?

56:03.485 --> 56:05.695
- [student chatter]
- [gentle music]

56:12.535 --> 56:14.037
You broke up with Ung, didn't you?

56:15.246 --> 56:17.791
And you two were dating
for such a long time.

56:19.042 --> 56:22.587
Hey, come on.
You can be honest with me, you know that.

56:22.670 --> 56:25.340
Just tell me if you're feeling any pain.

56:25.423 --> 56:28.802
It's scarier seeing you act like this.
As if nothing's wrong.

56:28.885 --> 56:30.386
It's so hard to watch this.

56:30.470 --> 56:32.347
Don't worry about it too much.

56:34.390 --> 56:35.934
But are you really okay?

56:37.268 --> 56:38.186
Hmm.

56:38.686 --> 56:40.063
I swear, I'm really okay.

56:42.899 --> 56:44.984
[gentle music continues]

56:49.906 --> 56:51.616
Hey, grandma, I'm home.

56:56.621 --> 56:57.580
[shoe thuds]

57:07.382 --> 57:09.050
[approaching footsteps]

57:16.224 --> 57:17.559
[thuds]

57:19.561 --> 57:20.645
[clicks]

57:21.813 --> 57:23.481
[tap running]

57:25.400 --> 57:27.277
[water echoing]

57:32.949 --> 57:34.993
[echoing fading to silence]

57:39.122 --> 57:41.916
["There For You" by Kim Na Young playing]

58:04.314 --> 58:06.900
["There For You"
by Kim Na Young continues]

58:18.703 --> 58:20.371
I tell you, I'm really fine.

58:21.206 --> 58:22.290
Yes, it's true.

58:25.376 --> 58:31.508
10 THINGS I HATE ABOUT YOU

58:32.509 --> 58:36.471
["There For You" continues]

58:53.154 --> 58:55.323
[upbeat outro music]

58:57.909 --> 58:59.536
[Yeon-su] Don't make me laugh.

58:59.619 --> 59:01.246
Is that what he said?

59:01.329 --> 59:02.247
[sighs]

59:02.330 --> 59:05.583
[Ung] The minor details may be different,
but to tell you the truth…

59:06.459 --> 59:09.587
It was on that day
when everything went haywire.

59:09.671 --> 59:10.588
Hey.

59:10.672 --> 59:13.341
[Yeon-su] Since you're pretty childish
and act like you're so pathetic…

59:13.424 --> 59:15.301
[both sigh]

59:15.969 --> 59:17.929
I believe you.

59:19.180 --> 59:20.932
[Ung] You also ruined my life.

59:21.015 --> 59:22.517
You wreaked havoc.
